[Reddit](https://reddit.com/submit?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.newscientist.com%2Farticle%2Fmg23731601-200-no-sweat-are-sports-drinks-worth-the-money%2F&title=No%20sweat%3A%20Are%20sports%20drinks%20worth%20the%20money%3F)
[Email](mailto:?subject=No%20sweat%3A%20Are%20sports%20drinks%20worth%20the%20money%3F&body=Dehydration%20is%20bad%2C%20and%20electrolytes%20are%20important.%20Sports%20drinks%20replace%20essential%20ions%20lost%20through%20sweat%20%E2%80%93%20but%20is%20that%20all%20just%20marketing%20hype%3F%0D%0Aread%20more:%20https%3A%2F%2Fwww.newscientist.com%2Farticle%2Fmg23731601-200-no-sweat-are-sports-drinks-worth-the-money%2F)

![Lucozade sign](https://images.newscientist.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/09111232/e9pry0.jpg)

Shaun Daley / Alamy

It’s hydrating, packed full of sugars and contains electrolytes vital for cell function. Which is why, until the mid-20th century, beer was considered the sports drink of choice – especially as it was [safer to drink than tap water](https://www.academia.edu/7065151/Beer_breaks_during_the_Tour_de_France._Some_observations_on_beer_and_cycling_in_the_early_1900s).

### No sweat: [The smart guide to exercise](/round-up/no-sweat/?intcmp=PAC|NSNS|2018-inlinelink_drinks&utm_medium=PAC&utm_source=NSNS&utm_campaign=inlinelink_drinks)

#### Forget the latest fad – here’s our evidence-based guide to workout success, and the truth about the advice you can ignore

Today, sports drinks have taken on a very different flavour. And if you believe the advertising, working out without one will lead to dehydration, impaired performance and a deep sense of self-loathing. But should…

